  "reason": "User-requested desktop sidebar optimization: in-place group disclosure, structural folder projection reuse with event invalidation, split pane width control, distinct count/action slots, and layout-free origin overscroll check. Mobile navigation behavior retained. Desktop main search bar and its existing actions now sit above the results, as requested by the user. User requested desktop-sidebar-only popup positioning and a top navigation command rail reusing the mobile navigation controls. User reports continued lag and an unwanted held-mouse fill on desktop sidebar folder/disclosure clicks: remove only its pressed fill, avoid unchanged row and page rewrites, coalesce the sidebar projection before paint, and acknowledge already applied sidebar state without a redundant scroll-layout read. User reports folder switching and disclosure still lag and requests removing redundant filter-list ellipses: reconcile tree rows after removing obsolete descendants, reuse the exact numeric Chinese collator, hide desktop-sidebar group management buttons and preserve their actions in the context menu. Capture desktop-sidebar selection scroll before result writes and consume/expire it within the same queued projection, avoiding a forced layout read after the result commit while retaining live session capture and explicit restoration. User requested whole-sidebar optimization: suppress unchanged desktop navigation presentation writes while preserving accessible labels, reuse unchanged group decoration with preference invalidation, and limit sidebar popup positioning to scrolls moving the leaf or its live/parent anchors. User requested continued product audit: keep an empty desktop toolbar hidden without redundant toggles; cancel stale divider drags on host resize and resynchronize actual/accessible width after commit or cancellation. No public prototype changes in this round.",
